---
// Financial Statements Lab: markup only. Behavior lives in src/scripts/tools/financial-statements.js
import { ANS, FORMULA, H2, H3, HINT, LOWER, PANEL, PRESETS, PROSE, QS, REVEAL, TOOL, VERDICT } from '../../scripts/lib/ui.js';
---
<div class={TOOL} data-tool="financial-statements">
  <section class="grid grid-cols-[400px_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-[18px] items-start max-[860px]:grid-cols-1">
    <div class={PANEL} aria-label="Transactions">
      <h2 class={H2} data-r="title">Business</h2>
      <div class={PRESETS} data-presets role="group" aria-label="Choose a business"></div>
      <p class:list={[HINT, PROSE]}>This month's transactions. Uncheck one to see what happens without it, or change an amount. Point at a transaction to see which lines it touches.</p>
      <ol class="list-none m-0 p-0 grid gap-1" data-r="tx"></ol>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-panel border border-line rounded-[10px] p-[18px] grid gap-3.5 content-start min-w-0">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 items-start max-[620px]:grid-cols-1 min-[861px]:max-[1080px]:grid-cols-1">
        <section class="border border-line rounded-lg p-3 grid gap-2 min-w-0" aria-labelledby="fs-is-h">
          <header class="flex gap-2.5 items-center"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-accent text-panel font-mono font-semibold text-[13px] leading-[normal] grid place-items-center shrink-0">1</span><div><h3 class={H3} id="fs-is-h">Income statement</h3><span class="text-[12px] text-muted" data-r="period"></span></div></header>
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[13.5px]"><tbody data-r="is"></tbody></table>
        </section>
        <section class="border border-line rounded-lg p-3 grid gap-2 min-w-0" aria-labelledby="fs-oe-h">
          <header class="flex gap-2.5 items-center"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-accent text-panel font-mono font-semibold text-[13px] leading-[normal] grid place-items-center shrink-0">2</span><div><h3 class={H3} id="fs-oe-h">Statement of owner's equity</h3><span class="text-[12px] text-muted" data-r="period"></span></div></header>
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[13.5px]"><tbody data-r="oe"></tbody></table>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section class="border border-line rounded-lg p-3 grid gap-2 min-w-0" aria-labelledby="fs-bs-h">
        <header class="flex gap-2.5 items-center"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-accent text-panel font-mono font-semibold text-[13px] leading-[normal] grid place-items-center shrink-0">3</span><div><h3 class={H3} id="fs-bs-h">Balance sheet</h3><span class="text-[12px] text-muted" data-r="asof"></span></div></header>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 items-start max-[620px]:grid-cols-1 min-[861px]:max-[1080px]:grid-cols-1">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[13.5px]"><tbody><tr><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="2" class="text-left font-semibold pt-2 pb-[3px] pr-1 pl-0 text-[13px] border-b border-line">Assets</th></tr></tbody><tbody data-r="bs-a"></tbody></table>
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[13.5px]"><tbody data-r="bs-l"></tbody></table>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class={VERDICT} data-r="verdict" role="status"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class={LOWER}>
    <div class={PANEL}>
      <h2 class={H2}>How the statements connect</h2>
      <div class={FORMULA}>Revenue − Expenses = Net income<span>Start capital + Investments + Net income − Withdrawals = End capital</span><span>Assets = Liabilities + End capital</span></div>
      <p>Build them in order. The <span class="bg-accent/14 rounded px-1 font-semibold">net income</span> from the income statement moves to the statement of owner's equity. The <span class="bg-good/16 rounded px-1 font-semibold">ending capital</span> from that statement moves to the balance sheet. That's why the balance sheet always balances.</p>
    </div>
    <div class={PANEL}>
      <h2 class={H2}>Try it</h2>
      <ol class={QS}>
        <li>Uncheck the owner's withdrawal. Which statements change, and which one doesn't? <button type="button" class={REVEAL} data-reveal>Hint</button><span class={ANS} hidden>The statement of owner's equity and the balance sheet change. The income statement doesn't, because a withdrawal is not an expense.</span></li>
        <li>Uncheck the supplier payment. Why doesn't net income change, even though cash went up? <button type="button" class={REVEAL} data-reveal>Hint</button><span class={ANS} hidden>Paying a bill isn't an expense. It lowers cash and accounts payable by the same amount, so only the balance sheet changes.</span></li>
        <li>Raise the rent until the business shows a net loss. Does the balance sheet still balance? <button type="button" class={REVEAL} data-reveal>Hint</button><span class={ANS} hidden>Yes. A net loss lowers capital, and the extra cash paid lowers assets by the same amount.</span></li>
        <li>Which transactions change cash but not net income? Which change net income but not cash? <button type="button" class={REVEAL} data-reveal>Hint</button><span class={ANS} hidden>Loans, supplier payments, investments, and withdrawals change cash only. Sales on account and using up supplies change net income without touching cash.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script>
  import { initFinancialStatements } from '../../scripts/tools/financial-statements.js';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-tool="financial-statements"]').forEach(initFinancialStatements);
</script>
